rustaceanvim: standalone files and non-rustup sysroots

- Standalone .rs files share one client that lists them in rust-analyzer's
  linkedProjects (reloaded on didChangeConfiguration), instead of attaching to
  the first client as an extra workspace folder, which never analyses them
  (https://github.com/mrcjkb/rustaceanvim/issues/190).
- Cargo workspaces are never added to the standalone client, nor standalone
  directories to a Cargo client.
- Standard library sources under */lib/rustlib/src/rust/ (fenix, nixpkgs)
  reuse the active client, as ~/.rustup toolchains already do, instead of
  adding library/ as a workspace.

